# .audit artifacts (JSON only)

All runtime files under `.audit/` in the **target repository** must be **formatted JSON** (2-space indent, trailing newline). No YAML, no Markdown reports in this folder.

## Layout

```
<target-repo>/.audit/
├── profile.json            # stack profile (audit-init)
└── reports/
    ├── latest.json         # consolidated audit report
    └── <dimension>.json    # per-skill findings (architecture, security, …)
```

JSON Schemas live **only in this catalog** under `skills/<skill>/assets/*.schema.json` — never copied into `.audit/`.

## Conventions

| Rule | Detail |
|------|--------|
| Format | `JSON.stringify(data, null, 2) + '\n'` |
| Schema | `skills/<skill>/assets/<artifact>.schema.json` — source of truth in the skill folder |
| Validation | Scripts validate against the skill's schema before writing to `.audit/` |
| Provenance | Every artifact includes `generatedBy`: `https://github.com/sergeychernov/repo-audit-skills.git` (import from `skills/_shared/generated-by.mjs`) |
| Read order | Downstream skills read `.audit/profile.json` first; never re-detect stack |

## Git

- Commit `profile.json` when sharing audit context across the team.
- Add `.audit/reports/` to `.gitignore` if reports are ephemeral.
